# AVI ELF II / Hyperboard bench-test ROM. Q/EF default, optional 1854.
# Comments beginning with # are ignored by romtext.
AVI ELF II / HYPERBOARD - BENCH TEST ROM
Start: Q/EF3 serial console, press CR at 2400 baud.
UART command changes to experimental CDP1854 COM2 9600 8N1.
A RESET returns to Q/EF3; see docs/AVI_FIRST_BENCH_TEST.md.

PROGRAM CONTROL
    CALL addr               -- SCRT call
    RUN [addr]              -- execute with P=0
    CONT[inue]              -- resume from break

LANGUAGES (PENDING REAL HARDWARE TEST)
    BAS[ic] [NEW|OLD]      -- rc/BASIC Level 2
    ASM [NEW|OLD]         -- editor/assembler

MEMORY / I-O
    E[xamine] addr [end]   -- read memory
    D[eposit] addr data..  -- change memory
    IN[put] port           -- read 1802 I/O port
    OU[tput] port data     -- write 1802 I/O port
    :llaaaattdddd..cc      -- Intel HEX upload

DIAGNOSTICS
    UART                   -- EXPERIMENTAL CDP1854 9600 8N1
    SH[ow] EF              -- read EF1..EF4
    TE[st] RAM            -- RAM test
    HEL[p]                 -- this text

NOT IMPLEMENTED: Tiny BASIC, cassette, Visual/02, Forth.
RTC/NVR, IDE/BOOT and 8250-UART paths are disabled.
Before UART: verify Hyperboard jumpers and 1854/1863 clocks.
